<title>USA: Organogenesis gets Graftpatch clearance.</title>
<headline>Organogenesis gets Graftpatch clearance.</headline>
<dateline>CANTON, Mass. 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Organogenesis Inc said Friday it received marketing clearance from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for its Graftpatch soft tissue reinforcement product.</p>
<p>The company said Graftpatch was cleared for use in general surgical procedures to reinforce soft tissue. Organogenesis said about one million soft tissue surgical procedures, including hernia and bladder repair, are performed each year in the U.S.</p>
<p>Organogenesis said it has three U.S. patents issued or pending that apply to Graftpatch.</p>
<p>Organogenesis said it intends to market the product through a partner with an established presence in the hospital/surgical market. The company said it would manufacture Graftpatch.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610))</p>
